Fix the nct6687d out-of-tree fan driver for Linux 7.2.

WHY THIS EXISTS
The BC-250's fan is driven by nct6687d (github.com/Fred78290/nct6687d), built by
DKMS. On 7.2 it stops building:

  nct6687.c:476:9: error: implicit declaration of function 'strncpy'

strncpy() is gone from <linux/string.h> - it now appears there only in comments,
as the function other helpers replace - and the kernel compiles with -Werror on
implicit declarations, so this is an error, not a warning.

strscpy() does exactly what the call needed (truncate and always terminate) and
has existed for years, so the patched source still builds for 7.1.7 and older.
That matters: DKMS keeps one source tree for every installed kernel.

WHY IT IS NOT A KERNEL PATCH
The module is not in the kernel tree. The source is vendored under
/usr/src/nct6687d-1.0 on the board and travels into the images from there, so
the fix is applied to that copy. This file exists so a rebuild from upstream
does not silently lose it - without the fix the board boots with no fan control
and no tacho, and nothing says why.

    cd /usr/src/nct6687d-1.0 && patch -p0 < nct6687d-strscpy-7.2.patch
    dkms build -m nct6687d -v 1.0 -k <kernel> && dkms install -m nct6687d -v 1.0 -k <kernel>

--- nct6687.c.orig	2026-05-30 13:54:45.748753243 +0200
+++ nct6687.c	2026-08-18 23:25:08.749949524 +0200
@@ -37,6 +37,10 @@
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
+// 18/08/2026: dal kernel 7.2 <linux/string.h> non arriva piu' per traverso,
+// e il kernel compila con -Werror sulle dichiarazioni implicite: senza questa
+// riga strncpy() e' un errore, non un avviso, e il modulo non si costruisce.
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>
 
 #define DRVNAME "nct6687"
@@ -473,7 +477,12 @@
 	char valcp[16];
 	char *s;
 
-	strncpy(valcp, val, 16);
+	// 18/08/2026: dal kernel 7.2 strncpy() non esiste piu' - in string.h resta
+	// solo nominata come "funzione sostituita" - e il kernel compila con -Werror
+	// sulle dichiarazioni implicite, quindi il modulo non si costruiva. strscpy fa
+	// esattamente quel che serviva qui (tronca e termina sempre) ed esiste da anni,
+	// quindi il sorgente resta buono anche per il 7.1.7.
+	strscpy(valcp, val, sizeof(valcp));
 	valcp[15] = '\0';
 
 	s = strstrip(valcp);
